401-
402-- same-origin pages and API, no permissive CORS
403-- strict Host and Origin checks, CSRF protection for mutations, request-body limits, security response headers, and bounded concurrent streams
404-- safe cookies or an equivalent per-process session mechanism where browser state is required
405-- path containment, artifact allowlisting, secret redaction, and safe error projection identical in strength to CLI/TUI behavior
406-- no hosted authentication, team permissions, tenant isolation, or remote-worker protocol in Phase 4
