128-## 4.1 Application Surface Requirements
129-
130-The `internal/app` package is the composition boundary for local interfaces. It should provide:
131-
132-- shared dependency construction for workspace discovery, config loading, runtime setup, and service creation
133-- typed use-case functions for project, sprint, study, code extraction, validation, status, flow, execute, review, smoke, and verify operations
134-- CLI adapters that parse arguments, call use cases, and render text/JSON
135-- TUI adapters that translate key actions into the same use cases and render terminal models
136-- Web adapters that map HTTP requests to the same use cases and render HTML, JSON, or SSE without owning product behavior
137-
138-The intended direction is:
139-
140-```text
141-cmd/ultraplan -> internal/app -> product modules/platform
142-internal/tui  -> internal/app -> product modules/platform
143-internal/web  -> internal/app -> product modules/platform
144-```
145-
146-Avoid this direction:
147-
148-```text
149-internal/tui -> CLI command handlers -> stdout parsing
150-internal/tui -> os/exec("ultraplan", ...)
151-internal/web -> CLI command handlers or os/exec("ultraplan", ...)
152-```
153-
154-Subprocess execution is acceptable only for explicit external runtime behavior already owned by `platform/runtime` and `agentwrap`, not for UltraPlan calling itself.
155-
156-## 5. Workspace Requirements
--
2211-
2212-- same-host multi-process versus shared-filesystem multi-host support and the guarantees at that boundary
2213-- dedicated coordinator/daemon, fenced direct repository writers, or a hybrid
2214:- filesystem snapshot/journal, SQLite, agentwrap store composition, or another smallest sufficient durable mechanism
2215-- interface/package ownership without moving workflow semantics out of study/sprint modules or duplicating agentwrap
2216-- worker cancellation versus safe adoption after owner loss
2217-- run/attempt/stage/task identity hierarchy and correlation format
2218-- lease duration, heartbeat cadence, clock assumptions, fencing, and process-birth verification
